This github repository contains a few astrophysical simulations.

The first one solves for the equation of motion of a a test particle in Schwarzschild space-time usinng the the SChwarzschild 
and also computes the Innermost Stable Circular Orbit.

The second one simulates molecular cloud dynamics using SPH.

The third one computes graviational forces for N-body problem based on a hierarchial approach.

The fourth one solves for the Flux in the accretion around a blackhole using Newtonian gravity.

The fifth one applies General Relativistic correction to the fourth one.

The sixth one computes the evolution of scale factor of the universe with time for different values of cosmological parameters.

The seventh one computes the Connection coefficients, Rieman Tensor, Ricci Tensor and Scalar Curavature for a given metric 
(here, it is the Schwarzschild Metric).

The ninth one does the following: create a map with random galaxy distribution, 
Determine galaxy count at a given flux in far-infrared to build a map of Poisson distribution of galaxies, 
Spatially correlate the sources using the power spectrum of the CIB.
